WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.160 --> 00:00:10.720
Having an assignment to write a research paper&nbsp;
may be in the same category as a dentist telling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:15.280
you that you need a root canal, neither will be&nbsp;
painless but each can be made less painful when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:21.200
having a positive attitude and knowing what to&nbsp;
expect. The analogy that writing a research paper&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:26.800
is like a marathon rather than like a sprint&nbsp;
race is frequently used. It’s time consuming,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:32.480
it doesn't always go smoothly and can even be&nbsp;
painful at times. But understanding and applying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:37.120
what needs to be done before, during and after&nbsp;
will help you run that research writing race.&nbsp;

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:43.840
This course will help you understand the&nbsp;
writing decisions that will need to be made.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:50.160
And to anticipate potential barriers, so you&nbsp;
can take steps to either avoid, if possible,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.160 --> 00:00:55.680
the problem areas, or at least to minimize&nbsp;
them. The writing process is emphasized in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:55.680 --> 00:01:01.920
every writing course. As with any process, enough&nbsp;
time needs to be allowed for each step or stage.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:07.360
The lessons in this course will help you realize&nbsp;
the importance of managing your time throughout&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:13.280
the entire process. Also, all three of the&nbsp;
pre-writing methods are discussed and illustrated.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:18.240
And then you'll learn how that pre-writing stage&nbsp;
will help you prepare a structured outline.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:24.880
We'll look at how you can select a research worthy&nbsp;
topic. And how to turn that idea into a strong&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:31.920
thesis statement. And then how to select research&nbsp;
to support that thesis. How much, how to find it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:37.440
what sources are credible and how to document&nbsp;
those sources. And finally, the course will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:43.520
emphasize the importance of the revision process.&nbsp;
So, let’s begin on the research paper journey.&nbsp;

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:51.200
Why is publishing important?
If you're a graduate student,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.200 --> 00:01:56.400
you may ask yourself, to do or not to&nbsp;
do a PhD? What will happen if I follow&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:02.000
that track? You have just begun your PhD and&nbsp;
wondering how to present your research right.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:07.280
In which genre should you publish? 
 
For starters, you should know that one&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:07.280 --> 00:02:11.280
of the main tasks of the researcher is to&nbsp;
spread their work and present it to peers.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:17.520
We need to understand academia and how publishing&nbsp;
is a very critical component for a researcher&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:22.480
to advance the scientific knowledge. 
 
Publication is a form of expression and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:27.840
communication. By putting your ideas together&nbsp;
in a resourceful way and publishing it,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:33.040
it allows you to share your results. If&nbsp;
scientists kept their results in the lab,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:38.240
there will be no real-world progress.
 
Publication can also help you feel stronger&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:42.960
about your work by getting important criticism&nbsp;
back from reviewers who are experts in your field.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:49.520
It also enables you to get familiar with other&nbsp;
academics working on your topic. Furthermore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.520 --> 00:02:55.600
if you are thinking about continuing your academic&nbsp;
life, publishing is extremely important. You will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.600 --> 00:03:01.440
be evaluated in terms of number of publication&nbsp;
and in which kinds of journals you publish. It&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:01.440 --> 00:03:06.720
contributes to determining salaries, academic&nbsp;
position, contracts, and grants application.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:10.960
The good things about research is&nbsp;
that there is no one standard way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:17.840
This means there are many ways to share your work&nbsp;
and to get published depending on your domain.&nbsp;

00:03:19.440 --> 00:03:23.280
The main difference between research&nbsp;
papers and other forms of publishing&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:27.040
is that research papers are often&nbsp;
strengthened by facts and statistics. 
 &nbsp;

00:03:28.000 --> 00:03:32.960
There are different types of scholarly literature,&nbsp;
some of which require original research,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:38.000
also regarded as primary literature, and some&nbsp;
that are based on other published work or known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:43.440
as secondary literature. It is important to&nbsp;
have a clear idea about the different types of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.440 --> 00:03:48.400
articles that you can publish in journals. This&nbsp;
will help you understand the ways in which you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.400 --> 00:03:52.800
can disseminate your work and identify what kind&nbsp;
of article would be suitable for your study.   
 &nbsp;

00:03:53.680 --> 00:03:59.200
The types of publications are different in&nbsp;
different fields. For instance, a clinical trial&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:04.240
is possible only in the field of medicine, while&nbsp;
an empirical study is more common in the field of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:10.160
social sciences. It is important to remember that&nbsp;
not all journals publish every kind of article.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:11.120 --> 00:04:14.800
Therefore, most journal publishers&nbsp;
provide prospective authors with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.800 --> 00:04:18.160
accurate and specific guidelines for&nbsp;
the different articles they publish.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:23.520
Specifications about the types of articles&nbsp;
published can be found under the guidelines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:28.480
to authors section on a journal’s website.&nbsp;
If you have a target journal in mind,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:32.160
you should check whether it publishes the&nbsp;
kind of manuscript you are planning to write.
 &nbsp;

00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:36.240
Some of the possible types of&nbsp;
scientific publications are:&nbsp;

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:40.320
Original research ,
Review article ,&nbsp;

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:43.600
Clinical case study ,
Clinical trial ,&nbsp;

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:47.440
Perspective, opinion, and commentary ,
and Book review.&nbsp;

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.760
Original Articles
Original articles are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:59.280
papers that detailed studies reporting original&nbsp;
research and are classified as primary literature.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:05.760
They include hypothesis, background study,&nbsp;
methods, results, interpretation of findings,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.760 --> 00:05:11.520
and a discussion of possible implications. These&nbsp;
normally require a significant investment of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:14.880
time to collect the primary data&nbsp;
and interpret it conclusively.&nbsp;

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:20.720
Review article
Review articles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:25.520
provide a critical and constructive analysis&nbsp;
of existing published literature in a field,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:31.120
through summary, analysis, and comparison,&nbsp;
often identifying specific gaps or problems&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:31.120 --> 00:05:36.240
and providing recommendations for future&nbsp;
research. These are considered as secondary&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:40.800
literature since they generally do not present&nbsp;
new data from the author's experimental work.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:41.760 --> 00:05:47.840
Review articles can be of three types: literature&nbsp;
reviews, systematic reviews, and meta-analyses.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:53.440
Review articles can be of varying lengths&nbsp;
depending upon the journal and subject area.&nbsp;

00:05:56.560 --> 00:06:01.200
Clinical case study
Clinical case studies present the details of real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:06.960
patient cases from medical or clinical practice.&nbsp;
The cases presented are usually those that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:13.040
contribute significantly to the existing knowledge&nbsp;
on the field. The study is expected to discuss the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:19.680
signs, symptoms, diagnosis, and treatment of a&nbsp;
disease. Clinical case studies require a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:19.680 --> 00:06:24.880
practical experience and may not be a suitable&nbsp;
publication format for early career researchers.&nbsp;

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:30.800
Clinical trial
Clinical trials describe the methodology,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:36.080
implementation, and results of controlled studies,&nbsp;
usually undertaken with large patient groups.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:40.480
Clinical trials often require&nbsp;
practical work experience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.480 --> 00:06:43.360
as well as high standards&nbsp;
of ethics and reliability.&nbsp;

00:06:46.560 --> 00:06:51.920
Perspective, opinion, and commentary
Perspective pieces are scholarly reviews&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:51.920 --> 00:06:57.840
of fundamental concepts or prevalent ideas&nbsp;
in a field. These are usually essays that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:02.080
present a personal point of view critiquing&nbsp;
widespread notions pertaining to a field.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:07.680
A perspective piece can be a review of a&nbsp;
single concept or a few related concepts.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:14.320
These are considered as secondary literature.&nbsp;
Opinion articles present the author’s viewpoint&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:14.320 --> 00:07:20.080
on the interpretation, analysis, or methods&nbsp;
used in a particular study. It allows the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.600
author to comment on the strength and&nbsp;
weakness of a theory or hypothesis.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:31.040
Opinion articles are usually based on constructive&nbsp;
criticism and should be backed by evidence. Such&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.040 --> 00:07:36.560
articles promote discussion on current issues&nbsp;
concerning science. Commentaries are short&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:36.560 --> 00:07:41.280
articles that draw attention to or present a&nbsp;
criticism of a previously published article,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:41.280 --> 00:07:46.400
book, or report, explaining why it interested&nbsp;
them and how it might be illuminating for readers.&nbsp;

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:53.760
Finally , Book review
Book reviews are published&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:59.520
in most academic journals. The aim of a book&nbsp;
review is to provide insight and opinion on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:59.520 --> 00:08:05.600
recently published scholarly books. Book reviews&nbsp;
are a good publication option for early-career&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:10.080
researchers as it allows the researcher to&nbsp;
stay abreast of new literature in the field,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:12.800
while at the same time, adding&nbsp;
to his publication list.&nbsp;

00:08:14.560 --> 00:08:19.520
Which is easier to publish ? An original&nbsp;
research article or a review article?&nbsp;

00:08:21.040 --> 00:08:25.360
A review article is generally more difficult&nbsp;
to publish for the simple reason that it is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.360 --> 00:08:29.920
more difficult to write a good quality review&nbsp;
than a good quality original research paper.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.880 --> 00:08:34.400
A good review is not just a&nbsp;
summary of the existing literature;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:34.400 --> 00:08:40.240
it has to be really critical and should provide&nbsp;
a direction or perspective for future research.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:45.440
This perspective often develops with maturity and&nbsp;
long standing experience of working in the field.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:46.400 --> 00:08:50.560
In fact, some of the best reviews come&nbsp;
from well-respected experts in the field.
 &nbsp;

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:55.440
However, it also depends on the kind of&nbsp;
review article you are planning to write.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:01.760
For a narrative review or a literature review,&nbsp;
expertise and experience is more important.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.720 --> 00:09:07.360
If you are planning to write a systematic&nbsp;
review, you need not be an expert in the field;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.360 --> 00:09:11.120
if you have a good question, and if&nbsp;
the review is properly performed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:11.120 --> 00:09:16.800
your article will be of good quality. But then&nbsp;
again, a systematic review takes a lot of time. 
 &nbsp;

00:09:17.760 --> 00:09:22.320
If you are thinking in terms of easy&nbsp;
publication, I would say an original research&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:22.320 --> 00:09:27.440
article will be a better choice than a review&nbsp;
article. However, remember that what matters&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:35.840
the most is the quality of your research and how&nbsp;
well you have presented it in your manuscript.

